    <!-- PRIVACY POLICY -->
    <h2>1. Privacy Policy</h2>

    <h3>1.1. Who we are</h3>
    <p>
      This Privacy Policy explains how the <strong>Is It AI?</strong> mobile
      application (the “App”) handles information. The App is developed and
      published by an independent developer based in Spain (“we”, “us”, “our”).
    </p>

    <h3>1.2. What the App does</h3>
    <p>
      Is It AI? is a casual educational game where users guess whether images,
      videos, or content are generated by artificial intelligence or created by
      humans. The App is designed purely for entertainment and awareness
      purposes and does not provide professional, legal, or scientific advice.
    </p>

    <h3>1.3. Data we collect directly</h3>
    <p>
      We do <strong>not</strong> require account registration or login. We do
      <strong>not</strong> directly collect, store, or sell personal data such as
      names, email addresses, phone numbers, or precise locations.
    </p>

    <h3>1.4. Advertising & third-party data collection (AdMob)</h3>
    <p>
      The App is monetized using the Google Mobile Ads SDK (AdMob). Specifically:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Two banner ads</li>
      <li>One interstitial ad shown at natural breaks in gameplay</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Google, as a third-party advertising provider, may automatically collect
      certain information to deliver and measure ads, including:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Approximate location (derived from IP address)</li>
      <li>Advertising identifiers</li>
      <li>App interaction data (screens viewed, ad impressions, clicks)</li>
      <li>Performance and diagnostics data (crash reports, loading times)</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      This data is processed by Google in accordance with its own
      <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Privacy Policy</a>
      and
      <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/ads" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Ads Policy</a>.
    </p>

    <h3>1.5. Purpose of processing</h3>
    <p>
      Data processed through AdMob may be used for:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Displaying contextual or personalized ads</li>
      <li>Measuring ad effectiveness</li>
      <li>Analytics and app stability</li>
      <li>Fraud prevention and security</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>1.6. Legal basis (EEA / UK)</h3>
    <p>
      For users located in the European Economic Area or the United Kingdom,
      certain data processing (such as personalized advertising) is based on
      user consent. Where required, the App displays a consent dialog using
      Google’s User Messaging Platform (UMP).
    </p>

    <h3>1.7. Children’s privacy</h3>
    <p>
      The App is intended for users aged <strong>16 and older</strong>, or for
      use under parental or guardian supervision in accordance with local law.
      We do not knowingly collect personal data from children.
    </p>

    <h3>1.8. Data sharing & international transfers</h3>
    <p>
      We do not sell personal data. Advertising data is processed by Google and
      its partners and may be transferred to servers outside your country. Please
      refer to Google’s documentation for details on safeguards.
    </p>

    <h3>1.9. User controls</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Adjust ad personalization settings in your device privacy settings</li>
      <li>Reset or remove your advertising ID</li>
      <li>Use the in-app consent dialog (if shown)</li>
      <li>Uninstall the App at any time</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>1.10. Security</h3>
    <p>
      We do not operate our own backend or user database. AdMob data is
      transmitted using industry-standard security measures. However, no system
      is completely secure.
    </p>

    <h3>1.11. Policy updates</h3>
    <p>
      This Privacy Policy may be updated from time to time. Changes will be
      reflected by updating the effective date. Continued use of the App means
      acceptance of the updated policy.
    </p>

    <h3>1.12. Contact</h3>
    <p>
      If you have questions about this Privacy Policy, contact the developer at:
      <a href="mailto:shish.hamish@gmail.com">shish.hamish@gmail.com</a>
    </p>

